WEBVTT

00:07:58.413 --> 00:08:01.538
Teeth can tell us things
that the history books leave out.

00:08:01.579 --> 00:08:04.121
Our final story brings us
back closer to Mississippi

00:08:04.163 --> 00:08:06.704
to an abandoned cemetery
just west of Jackson,

00:08:06.746 --> 00:08:09.121
where we can learn
about the lives of the settlers

00:08:09.163 --> 00:08:10.829
who lived here in the early 1800s.

00:08:10.871 --> 00:08:12.579
Now, some of them came with wealth.

00:08:12.621 --> 00:08:16.871
They could erect tombstones and write
their life histories on their graves.

00:08:16.913 --> 00:08:19.246
If they were married,
whether they had children,

00:08:19.288 --> 00:08:21.829
where they came from
and sometimes even how they died,

00:08:21.871 --> 00:08:25.204
as cholera and yellow fever epidemics
swept through the region.

00:08:25.246 --> 00:08:29.288
Richard lived until age 56.
He died in 1849.